WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.634
-It is great to see you, bud.
-Happy to be here.

00:00:02.634 --> 00:00:04.033
-Welcome back to the show.

00:00:04.033 --> 00:00:05.467
And before we get into this,
I want to congratulate you.

00:00:05.467 --> 00:00:07.367
You have two little
babies now, right?

00:00:07.367 --> 00:00:11.434
-Two little babies, yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.434 --> 00:00:13.367
Congratulations.
-Yeah, the last time

00:00:13.367 --> 00:00:15.567
I was on Broadway, it was
a little different schedule.

00:00:15.567 --> 00:00:16.868
I didn't have -- you know,
I wasn't waking up so early

00:00:16.868 --> 00:00:18.200
the last time, yeah.
-Exactly.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:20.200
Yeah, it's a little --
Is it much tougher now?

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.767
-It's a little tougher now.
Yeah, but it's worth it.

00:00:22.767 --> 00:00:25.767
-What do the kids
think of daddy acting?

00:00:25.767 --> 00:00:28.300
-Oh, my daughter loves it.
My son? He's only 2.

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:29.801
I have a 6-year-old
and a 2-year-old.

00:00:29.801 --> 00:00:32.934
But Lucy's seen the show
a handful of times,

00:00:32.934 --> 00:00:36.267
and she loves it.
She wants to come every weekend.

00:00:36.267 --> 00:00:38.801
But the first time
she saw it, she saw me --

00:00:38.801 --> 00:00:41.000
I have to kiss
another woman in the show,

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:43.968
and the whole cast
was watching for her reaction.

00:00:43.968 --> 00:00:46.200
And she -- you know,
she was just properly horrified.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:49.167
She thought I was ending
my marriage,

00:00:49.167 --> 00:00:52.100
you know, in front of her.
Just ruining our family

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:53.334
right in front
of her little face.

00:00:53.334 --> 00:00:56.834
-Oh, no! Oh, my God.
-Yeah, it was very funny.

00:00:56.834 --> 00:00:59.534
-You know, I think about you
more than you know, because I --

00:00:59.534 --> 00:01:02.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:04.200
-Because I saw you
in "Hamilton," and, gosh,

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.467
you were unbelievable
in that job.

00:01:06.467 --> 00:01:07.667
You know that.
You won the Tony Award.

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:10.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:10.634 --> 00:01:14.901
You're the first face --
You're the first face --

00:01:14.901 --> 00:01:17.367
the first person to say
anything in the whole show.

00:01:17.367 --> 00:01:19.367
You start the whole show off.

00:01:19.367 --> 00:01:21.167
You -- like, when
that curtain opened,

00:01:21.167 --> 00:01:23.234
it's just you,
and I think about that.

00:01:23.234 --> 00:01:24.801
I go, that's so much pressure.

00:01:24.801 --> 00:01:26.834
And I've seen you
do it three times --

00:01:26.834 --> 00:01:28.501
I'm lucky enough
to see you do it three times --

00:01:28.501 --> 00:01:31.234
and you nail it
every single time.

00:01:31.234 --> 00:01:33.534
You are amazing.
Do you like that pressure?

00:01:33.534 --> 00:01:34.834
-Yeah.
I was thinking about you

00:01:34.834 --> 00:01:36.200
when I was doing that.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:37.534
-You were thinking about me?
-Yeah.

00:01:37.534 --> 00:01:40.567
-Wow.
-No, I -- I -- I do.

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:44.334
I just loved -- I loved
what Lin had written so much.

00:01:44.334 --> 00:01:46.734
The only reason
to come to the theater

00:01:46.734 --> 00:01:48.934
is for tremendous writing.

00:01:48.934 --> 00:01:51.000
You know, writing is king
in the theater,

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:52.634
and I couldn't have found
a better piece

00:01:52.634 --> 00:01:53.834
than "Hamilton" at that time.

00:01:53.834 --> 00:01:55.567
I couldn't have found
a better piece

00:01:55.567 --> 00:01:57.934
than Mr. Davis's
"Purlie Victorious."

00:01:57.934 --> 00:02:00.534
At this time,
it's so extraordinary.

00:02:00.534 --> 00:02:04.200
And so that's what gives me the
confidence to get out there.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:05.801
It's not 'cause I'm so great.

00:02:05.801 --> 00:02:09.334
It's because these great writers
are so great.

00:02:09.334 --> 00:02:10.667
-I don't know.
You're pretty great, buddy.

00:02:10.667 --> 00:02:12.434
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.434 --> 00:02:14.300
I have a picture of you
and your Tony Award here.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:17.300
Come on, now.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:19.033
-Yeah.
-They don't give these out

00:02:19.033 --> 00:02:20.100
to everybody, bud.

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:21.400
They don't give this
to everybody.

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:23.667
You crushed it.
-Thanks.

00:02:23.667 --> 00:02:26.067
-I wanted to ask you because
I think last month I saw you.

00:02:26.067 --> 00:02:29.200
You did a thing,
Broadway for Biden.

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:30.667
And the President
was there watching.

00:02:30.667 --> 00:02:32.234
And you teamed up
with Lin again.

00:02:32.234 --> 00:02:34.200
-Yeah.
It was the first time

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:36.868
we've sung together
in about seven years.

00:02:36.868 --> 00:02:38.534
You know, we're only like,
two years away

00:02:38.534 --> 00:02:42.200
from the 10-year
anniversary of "Hamilton,"

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:43.734
the "Hamilton" premiere
downtown.

00:02:43.734 --> 00:02:45.267
You know, you came downtown

00:02:45.267 --> 00:02:47.801
and just really gave us
such a boost.

00:02:47.801 --> 00:02:49.200
You know, you came
on the show

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:51.667
and you told the world
about this show that you'd seen.

00:02:51.667 --> 00:02:53.000
-Because Questlove told me

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:55.234
that it was at a public.
Right?

00:02:55.234 --> 00:02:56.667
-Yeah.
-And Quest was like,

00:02:56.667 --> 00:02:58.601
"You gotta go see this play,"
and I was like, "All right."

00:02:58.601 --> 00:03:00.534
And then, we went,
and I went with my wife,

00:03:00.534 --> 00:03:02.467
and she was like,
"I don't understand the rapping

00:03:02.467 --> 00:03:03.667
about Alexander Hamilton."

00:03:03.667 --> 00:03:05.167
I go, "I don't know."

00:03:05.167 --> 00:03:07.734
And, dude, we were crying
after your first thing.

00:03:07.734 --> 00:03:09.701
I was like, "This was
the greatest thing I ever saw."

00:03:09.701 --> 00:03:11.400
-Yeah.
-And that's 10 years ago?

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:12.801
-10 years, bro.
-Oh, my God.

00:03:12.801 --> 00:03:15.868
-Yeah. So we got together
for for a good cause,

00:03:15.868 --> 00:03:17.133
to raise some money
for the President.

00:03:17.133 --> 00:03:18.934
-Do you get nervous
around the President or...?

00:03:18.934 --> 00:03:21.000
-Terrified, but...
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:24.934
-But you also performed in front
of Obama and Michelle Obama.

00:03:24.934 --> 00:03:28.000
-That was -- that was
the most meaningful --

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:29.634
It wasn't --
The Tony night was great.

00:03:29.634 --> 00:03:30.934
Grammy night was great.

00:03:30.934 --> 00:03:33.467
But performing as an actor,
you know what I mean?

00:03:33.467 --> 00:03:36.000
Like, this is sometimes
a silly profession,

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:37.634
you know, let's be honest.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.634 --> 00:03:41.868
But, you know, that
it can be raised to that level

00:03:41.868 --> 00:03:44.767
that the leader
of the free world could make --

00:03:44.767 --> 00:03:48.033
you know, clear his schedule
for 45 minutes,

00:03:48.033 --> 00:03:50.868
that we might do something that
he thought was important enough

00:03:50.868 --> 00:03:54.567
to make time, you know,
it was just, um...

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:56.834
It was like --
I just think, like,

00:03:56.834 --> 00:04:00.167
that's what's possible,
you know, every now and again,

00:04:00.167 --> 00:04:01.000
when you're part of something
like that.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:02.334
-Anything's possible, yeah.

00:04:02.334 --> 00:04:04.300
Since "Hamilton,"
you've just been nonstop.

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:06.133
One of the hardest-working men
in show business.

00:04:06.133 --> 00:04:07.367
You're so talented.

00:04:07.367 --> 00:04:09.501
You have a new album
coming out November 17th.

00:04:09.501 --> 00:04:11.000
-Yes, sir.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:13.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:13.767 --> 00:04:18.634
But this one -- this one
is called "When a Crooner Dies"

00:04:18.634 --> 00:04:20.334
is the name of this album.

00:04:20.334 --> 00:04:22.133
Is this your fifth
or sixth album?

00:04:22.133 --> 00:04:24.167
-This is my fifth album.
-You have five albums, bud.

00:04:24.167 --> 00:04:27.400
-I do, yeah.
You know, most of the ones

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:29.934
that people know about
are the Christmas ones.

00:04:29.934 --> 00:04:31.534
But this is --
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.534 --> 00:04:33.000
This is --
I love those, too,

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:35.567
but this is all original music.
It's deeply personal,

00:04:35.567 --> 00:04:37.033
the most personal one.

00:04:37.033 --> 00:04:38.901
You know, when I started
making albums,

00:04:38.901 --> 00:04:41.200
my producer,
my best friend, my brother,

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:43.100
he told me,
"You know, at some point,

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:45.000
I don't want you to have
any more secrets.

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:47.734
I want you to whisper those
secrets onto these records."

00:04:47.734 --> 00:04:50.868
And so, yeah, it's been --
it's been a really

00:04:50.868 --> 00:04:53.868
wonderful thing
having this outlet,

00:04:53.868 --> 00:04:55.834
you know,
to be vulnerable and honest.

00:04:55.834 --> 00:04:58.067
-How do you
get the time to do all of it

00:04:58.067 --> 00:05:00.601
and have kids
and be on Broadway?

00:05:00.601 --> 00:05:02.667
I mean, this is --
And get rave reviews.

00:05:02.667 --> 00:05:05.801
I mean, congrats,
the play is doing great.

00:05:05.801 --> 00:05:07.601
You actually have
a little good news

00:05:07.601 --> 00:05:08.968
you can share
with the audience.

00:05:08.968 --> 00:05:12.400
-Yes. You know, theater is
still making its way back.

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:14.701
You know, I believe
in a healthy,

00:05:14.701 --> 00:05:16.601
thriving American theater

00:05:16.601 --> 00:05:19.200
for the good of our nation,
you know?

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:21.667
And so, this play
is doing so well,

00:05:21.667 --> 00:05:23.234
it's gotten such great response,

00:05:23.234 --> 00:05:25.300
we are extending
an additional month.

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:27.200
We will be at the Music Box
until February the 4th.

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:29.467
-Yes!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:29.467 --> 00:05:32.634
-Please buy a ticket.
-Go check this out.

00:05:32.634 --> 00:05:36.567
What do people --
what do people --

00:05:36.567 --> 00:05:39.367
What should they know
about "Purlie Victorious"?

00:05:39.367 --> 00:05:40.968
-Well, number one,
that it was written

00:05:40.968 --> 00:05:44.634
by a great American,
Mr. Ossie Davis.

00:05:44.634 --> 00:05:46.033
You know, he's like --
[ Applause ]

00:05:46.033 --> 00:05:47.667
Yeah, I mean --
-Yeah.

00:05:47.667 --> 00:05:50.367
You know, when you think about

00:05:50.367 --> 00:05:55.734
legendary, inspiring theatricals

00:05:55.734 --> 00:05:57.834
and writers and orators
in this country, you know,

00:05:57.834 --> 00:06:00.501
Ossie's got to be on your list.
And he wrote this play.

00:06:00.501 --> 00:06:04.467
It hasn't been on Broadway
since 1962.

00:06:04.467 --> 00:06:06.701
And it's -- it's about America.

00:06:06.701 --> 00:06:09.100
I think about Lin a lot
when I think about Mr. Davis,

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:11.667
you know, these young men
writing about their country,

00:06:11.667 --> 00:06:14.067
what it means,
what America means,

00:06:14.067 --> 00:06:15.767
what America meant to them.

00:06:15.767 --> 00:06:18.734
And it's a -- it's a really
surprisingly patriotic,

00:06:18.734 --> 00:06:20.934
joyful, moving experience.

00:06:20.934 --> 00:06:22.834
-Yeah.
Congratulations on this.

00:06:22.834 --> 00:06:24.968
And I'm going to check you out.
I'm just surprising you.

00:06:24.968 --> 00:06:26.634
And you'll see my reaction
when you kiss --

00:06:26.634 --> 00:06:28.300
when you kiss that person.
Be like -- [ Gasps ]

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:29.934
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:06:29.934 --> 00:06:32.300
Leslie Odom Jr., everybody.

00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:35.767
"Purlie Victorious"
is on Broadway right now.

00:06:35.767 --> 00:06:38.467
For tickets, go to
purlievictorious.com.

